---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: lessons.lessons
  size: 1
  alias: lesson
permalink: "/learn/{{ lesson.slug }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ lesson.title }}"
  seoTitle: "{{ lesson.title }}"
  description: "{{ lesson.description }}"
# The screens and buttons the closing line of every lesson page names, as the
# product spells them; each lesson's own names ride in data/lessons.json and
# tools/resources-coverage.js reads them from there (#742).
names: [Getting started]
---

{#- One lesson of the course as a page (#742): the mail's own words, in the
    article idiom. The subject is the title, the opener the first paragraph,
    the bullets a list, the close the last line, and then the same ending
    every article has, the free scan, because a reader here has no workspace
    to open the lesson's screen in. The lesson's own button lives in the
    product and in the mail; here its screen is named once, in the last
    line, so a reader who does have a workspace knows where to go. -#}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": {{ lesson.title | dump | safe }},
  "description": {{ lesson.description | dump | safe }},
  "datePublished": "{{ lessons.fetchedAt }}",
  "dateModified": "{{ lessons.fetchedAt }}",
  "author": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#organization" },
  "publisher": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#organization" },
  "image": "{{ site.url }}{{ '/assets/img/og.png' | asset }}",
  "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}" },
  "isAccessibleForFree": true,
  "isPartOf": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "{{ site.url }}/learn/", "name": "Learn Prospektor" },
  "articleSection": "learn",
  "inLanguage": "en"
}
</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "{{ site.name }}", "item": "{{ site.url }}/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Learn", "item": "{{ site.url }}/learn/" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": {{ lesson.subject | dump | safe }} }
  ]
}
</script>

<article class="res-article learn-lesson">

  <header class="res-hero">
    <div class="res-hero-inner">
      <a class="res-back" href="/learn/">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9.5 3.5L5 8l4.5 4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        Learn
      </a>
      <span class="tag">{{ lesson.topic }}</span>
      <h1 class="res-h1">{{ lesson.subject }}</h1>
      <div class="res-meta">
        <span>Day {{ lesson.day }} of {{ lessons.count }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="res-body">
    <div class="res-prose">
      <p>{{ lesson.opener }}</p>
      <ul>
        {%- for bullet in lesson.bullets %}
        <li>{{ bullet }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      <p>{{ lesson.close }}</p>
      <p class="learn-where">In the studio this is <a href="https://studio.prospektor.ai{{ lesson.path }}">{{ lesson.label | replace("Open the ", "the ") | replace("Open ", "") }}</a>. New here? Every workspace starts on Getting started.</p>
    </div>

    <aside class="res-cta">
      <span class="tag">try it</span>
      <h2>See this run on your own company</h2>
      <p>Prospektor reads a company's own website before it says anything about
        them (what they sell, to whom, and what changed recently), then scores fit
        and drafts what to send. The scan is free and takes about ninety seconds.</p>
      <a class="btn-cta" href="/#scan">Scan your site</a>
      <span class="res-cta-note">No account. No card. Nothing to install.</span>
    </aside>

    <nav class="learn-nav" aria-label="The course, in order">
      {%- if lesson.previous %}
      <a class="learn-nav-link" href="{{ lesson.previous.url }}">
        <span class="res-card-topic">Day {{ lesson.previous.day }}</span>
        <span class="res-more-title">{{ lesson.previous.subject }}</span>
      </a>
      {%- else %}<span></span>{%- endif %}
      {%- if lesson.next %}
      <a class="learn-nav-link learn-nav-next" href="{{ lesson.next.url }}">
        <span class="res-card-topic">Day {{ lesson.next.day }}</span>
        <span class="res-more-title">{{ lesson.next.subject }}</span>
      </a>
      {%- else %}
      <a class="learn-nav-link learn-nav-next" href="/learn/">
        <span class="res-card-topic">That is the course</span>
        <span class="res-more-title">Back to all eight</span>
      </a>
      {%- endif %}
    </nav>
  </div>

</article>
